<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Pressburg (1491)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1491">1491</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Pressburg (1491)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a> was signed on 7 November 1491 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladislaus-ii-of-hungary">Vladislaus II of Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and Emperor Frederick III and his son Maximilian. It ended Maximilian's war for the Hungarian throne after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a> and provided that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> would inherit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> if Vladislaus's line failed, as happened in 1526.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-pressburg-1491.jpg" alt="Treaty of Pressburg (1491)" width="320" height="271" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peace_of_Pressburg,_1491_(text_copy).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
